       "implemented": "A Baseline menu and Standard and Vibrant vertical Expressive command menus. They share measured placement, leading and trailing icons, wrapped labels, and bounded scrolling. The vertical menus use one to three named or unnamed groups, with gaps when they fit and a logical-trailing scrollbar when they overflow. A disabled command can receive focus and stays inactive. Selection and dismissal use caller messages. The legacy positioned popup keeps its skip-disabled policy. Vertical menus also support named command, single-choice, and multiple-choice groups. Single choices expose radio-menu state. Multiple choices expose checkbox-menu state. The caller owns the values. Keyboard movement keeps values unchanged until activation. Disabled choices preserve their checked state and cannot send actions. Submenus, system high contrast, and live screen-reader speech remain open.",
       "unit_evidence": "Material and Runtime tests cover visible trigger bounds, placement above or below, logical-edge mirroring, keyboard focus and reveal, rejection of disabled input, and click-through protection. Vertical menu tests cover both palettes, accessibility group order, pointer activation and focus return, and scrollbar geometry after resizing. Choice-menu tests cover named independent radio groups, retained focus and open state in multiple-choice groups, stable logical-leading checkmarks in both palettes, and disabled action rejection. Core tests verify that menu-radio metadata preserves the existing MenuItem role and serialization. macOS tests verify its separate accessibility role and action."
